# libc-test: musl's test suite, built as one program (docs/M13-PLAN.md,
# track P2) that runs the functional and regression sets on Jam OS. It is
# a system port (a test entry's program, no use on /data), in the boot
# image as usr/bin/libc-test; tools/libc-test.sh runs it. third_party/
# libc-test is the tree as upstream has it, less src/math/ (its data
# includes crlibm's LGPL tables, which this tree does not take). Each test
# is compiled as upstream writes it but for its tmpfile (files/shim.h) and
# linked into the one program with the runner (files/runner.c), which
# starts each as a child and compares the results with
# files/expected-failures.txt; api/ (compile-time header tests) and musl/
# are not built. The tests that need dynamic linking are not built.
name        libc-test
version     20260825
revision    1
summary     musl's libc-test suite as one program, run by tools/libc-test.sh
homepage    https://repo.or.cz/libc-test.git
category    tests
# "libc-test is developed as part of the musl project": MIT, in COPYRIGHT.
licence     MIT
licence-file COPYRIGHT
vendored    libc-test
place       boot
style       custom
host        python3
# Commit 7b95dfa5f5d5ca4d949221e0228ccc290bacc14e (2026-08-25).
program     bin/libc-test
